«
@@ ============================================================
@@ MeridLat — latitude from a meridian altitude, when the body bears due North
@@ or South.
@@ 
@@ Input : Ho Dec drn — observed altitude, declination, and the direction of the
@@         body, the text "S" or "N". Plain numbers are degrees; angles with a unit
@@         are accepted.
@@ Output: φ — latitude.
@@ ============================================================

  → hob dcl drn
  «
    IF drn "S" == drn "N" == OR NOT THEN "Direction must be S or N" DOERR END
    hob →Num IF DUP TypeName "unit" == THEN 1_° CONVERT UVAL END dcl →Num IF DUP TypeName "unit" == THEN 1_° CONVERT UVAL END
    → hox dcx
    «
      IF drn "S" == THEN dcx 90 + hox - ELSE dcx 90 - hox + END 1_° *
    »
  »
»
